Disclosure: research published by Wiz is one of these sources, and the site's author works at Wiz.
notes:
These are the primary sources the csoh.org kill chain cites. Every fact about the incident in this deck comes from that page, which draws on these.

Wiz Threat Research confirmed live secret leakage in dozens of cases; as the page discloses, the site's author works at Wiz. Endor Labs counted the public repositories that ran the action during the window and leaked secrets. Unit 42 is among the analysts who traced the foothold upstream through SpotBugs. CISA's advisory and the record for CVE-2025-30066 in NVD, the US National Vulnerability Database, complete the list.

The background slides name their own sources: the csoh.org GitHub Actions page and glossary, and MITRE ATT&CK.

